    "description": "``ZVAL`` is a C structure, that represents data in the PHP engine. It is a structure, which is never directly used from PHP code.\n\nIt may be access with ``debug_zval_dump()`` function, for debugging purposes. It is useful to debug PHP engine, or extensions.\n",
    "code": "<?php\n\n    // From the manual \n    $var1 = 'Hello';\n    $var1 .= ' World';\n    $var2 = $var1;\n    \n    debug_zval_dump($var1);\n    \n    // displays string(11) \"Hello World\" refcount(3)\n\n?>",
